hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18243","Affan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar Umayr ibn Yazid narrated to me, al-Harith ibn Fudayl and Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qurad, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing pilgrimage. He said: So I saw him come out of the privy and I followed him with the water skin or cup, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to relieve himself would go far. So I sat for him on the road until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, ablution. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and poured upon his hand and washed it, then he inserted his hand with its palm and poured upon one hand, then wiped over his head, then scooped water upon one hand, then wiped over his head, then scooped water scooping with his hand and struck it upon the back of his foot and wiped with his hand upon his foot, then he came and prayed the noon prayer for us."
